UNIT escape_property
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@c41c5fcd84e0 cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs escapeProperty, reproduced exactly. Independent anchor: GitHub's toolkit
  @actions/core@3.0.1 lib/command.js escapeProperty (driven through core.error's title property). Over text the two agree
  on 16914 of 16914 text inputs (the full generator at n = 20000 under mulberry32 seed 7, plus 15 targeted probes); they
  differ only on non-text arguments, which the primary's envelope excludes (the js files' widening, findings in the report).
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG escape_property(value: text) -> text
ENVELOPE text only: any length (including empty) and any well-formed Unicode — control characters (NUL included), letters
  of any script and astral characters are all in scope. Non-text arguments and text carrying an unpaired surrogate half are
  outside this envelope; the js and ts files widen it to both.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION Escape a value for use as a PROPERTY of a GitHub Actions workflow command (the file= and title= values in
  "::error file=<value>,title=<value>::message"), so that the value cannot end the property, start another property, end
  the property list or break the command line. Each of five characters becomes "%" followed by its two-digit uppercase
  hexadecimal code; the runner reverses exactly this mapping. One argument, no options.
BEHAVIOR
R1 The result is the input with every occurrence of a character in ESCAPES replaced by its replacement from that table,
  judged one code unit at a time with no context. Every other code unit is copied unchanged and in its original position.
R2 Empty text -> empty text.
R3 The percent sign is itself escaped, and replacements are never re-examined: an input that already contains an escape
  sequence ("%3A") is escaped again ("%253A"), so the operation is NOT idempotent and the runner's single unescape
  restores the original exactly.
R4 Carriage return and line feed are escaped independently: CRLF -> "%0D%0A", LF CR -> "%0A%0D".
R5 The equals sign, semicolon, quotes, backslash, solidus, space, tab, every other control character (NUL, VT, FF, NEL,
  U+2028, U+2029), the fullwidth colon and comma (U+FF1A, U+FF0C), every non-ASCII letter and astral characters are
  copied unchanged. CITED FIDELITY package — the escaped set is exactly ESCAPES, the same
  set as @actions/core@3.0.1.
TABLE ESCAPES — input code unit -> replacement text (R1); every replacement is three ASCII characters
  "%"  (U+0025, percent sign)     -> "%25"
  CR   (U+000D, carriage return)  -> "%0D"
  LF   (U+000A, line feed)        -> "%0A"
  ":"  (U+003A, colon)            -> "%3A"
  ","  (U+002C, comma)            -> "%2C"
INVARIANT length(result) = length(input) + 2 * (number of ESCAPES code units in input).
INVARIANT the result contains no CR, LF, colon or comma, so it can neither end the command line nor the property list,
  nor introduce another property.
ORACLE value -> oracles/escape_property.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 ff14a08e51b7415429531a615bac3b02c1ec17d6cde45c8701a1539dbba116d1
NOTE 24 frozen + 48 held-out, stamped once from the pinned authority (seed 1). 38 are language-neutral; 34 are js-only
  (three texts carrying an unpaired surrogate half; non-text arguments: none, bool, f64 including NaN/Infinity/-0, bigint, absent, list, map, boxed, RegExp, Set, byte
  array, Buffer; a missing argument; an extra second argument), routed by the tooling to the js envelope extension. Two of those
  are throws (a map whose conversion to text finds no callable method).
NOTE No rust variant. Cause: domain — the review system ships as JavaScript (rdv review and the rederive/sir-review GitHub
  Action); there is no Rust consumer.
SCOPE IN: R1-R5 over any text. OUT: escaping of the command MESSAGE (pr-review escapeData, which leaves colon and comma
  alone), assembly of the command line (pr-review annotations, including its unescaped line= value), and the anchor's
  omission of empty or falsy properties (an @actions/core issueCommand behavior, not part of property escaping).
PROVENANCE rederive@c41c5fcd84e0 (MIT), cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs line 119, export escapeProperty; seam
